&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NewsBreak&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local life runs on local information.&lt;/strong&gt; What happened down the street? Who can fix this? Where should we go tonight? NewsBreak started in 2015 to answer these questions, and today more than 40 million people a month rely on us to follow what’s going on in their zip code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three platforms with one vision: powering local life.&lt;/strong&gt; Led by founder and CEO Jeff Zheng, NewsBreak is our local life and news platform; Nearby AI connects people with local businesses; and NDot AI helps publishers and creators grow and earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building for the long term.&lt;/strong&gt; A $115 million Series C made us a unicorn in 2021, and we keep investing in our people. We’re Great Place to Work® certified and named to &lt;em&gt;Fast Company&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces for Innovators (2025) and &lt;em&gt;Fortune&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™ (2026).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Everyone makes an impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Whether you write code, shape products, tell our story, or run the business, we want people who own projects end to end, stay curious, and speak up. Join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at: NewsBreak, Nearby AI, NDot AI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NewsBreak is the nation&#39;s leading local news app, with one of the largest local audiences in the US. We&#39;re building something new on top of it: a lead generation platform for home-services businesses — roofing, HVAC, plumbing, landscaping, cleaning, remodeling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The product is live, not a deck. An AI agent interviews homeowners on the merchant&#39;s behalf, qualifies them (own vs. rent, service area, timing, project scope), and delivers scored leads with contact details attached. Merchants don&#39;t operate a tool or buy a retainer — they get leads. We build the merchant&#39;s custom intake conversation from their own website, automatically — which means your demo is their own branded lead page, generated live, before the first call ends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a founding GTM role. You&#39;ll be one of the first sellers on a new line of business inside a company with real distribution — which means your feedback sets the pricing, the packaging, and the playbook everyone after you runs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own merchant acquisition end-to-end in home services: prospect, pitch, close, onboard. Onboarding is minutes, not weeks — the product does the setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring relationships, not just dials. This market is over-cold-called; we&#39;re hiring books of business and referral networks, not phone scripts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the hard conversations. Lead-quality disputes, credits, saves, churn. If you&#39;ve never had a contractor tell you their leads were junk, this isn&#39;t the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close the loop with product. You&#39;ll talk to the team building the agent weekly; what merchants object to becomes what we build next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run pricing and packaging experiments — per-lead, subscription, hybrid. Nothing is sacred yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years selling to home-services contractors — lead generation, local digital marketing, or SaaS. Alumni of Angi Leads / HomeAdvisor, Networx, CraftJack, Modernize, eLocal, Service Direct, Thumbtack, Yelp, Scorpion, CAMP Digital, ServiceTitan, Housecall Pro strongly encouraged to apply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve sold recurring $200–$2,000/month spend to owner-operators, mostly by phone, and carried a retention number — not just a bookings number.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can walk us through, with specifics, how you handle &quot;your leads are garbage, I want a refund.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pipeline discipline and CRM hygiene. Early-stage means your numbers are the numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity: territories, pricing, and process are still being written — partly by you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to have: an active book of contractor relationships · familiarity with Nexstar Network / Service Nation / CertainPath communities · Spanish fluency&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base + uncapped commission · OTE and equity to be discussed based on experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product that actually delivers the thing contractors want — leads — backed by NewsBreak&#39;s local audience, not bought traffic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Founding-team influence on a business line, without startup payroll risk&lt;/li&gt;
