&lt;p&gt;Build the owned-audience growth infrastructure for the future of media.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a 0→1 product leader to own the NDot product roadmap and the publisher experience end to end. This is a highly customer-facing role: you&#39;ll spend real time in publisher meetings, work side-by-side with engineers on product and technical tradeoffs, and make the call on which customer requests should become reusable platform capabilities versus one-off custom work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be building reusable platform capabilities that can ultimately serve publishers and adjacent digital content businesses (e.g., short dramas), while sequencing that expansion deliberately rather than chasing every vertical at once.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run structured discovery with publishers to build a clear, evidence-based view of their priority needs, and translate that into a focused product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship visible improvements to the publisher portal and publisher experience (reporting, insights, and beyond).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the minimum product and integration required for lighthouse customers, and establish clear success metrics for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with engineering on architecture, APIs, data, and integrations — you&#39;ll need enough technical depth to be a real thought partner, not just a requirements-writer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a repeatable loop from customer feedback → prioritization → launch → measurement, and use it to productize the most valuable recurring needs across onboarding, analytics, engagement/growth, and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the platform so proven capabilities can extend to adjacent verticals without fragmenting the roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer discovery, product strategy, and prioritization skills, with real analytics chops and technical fluency across APIs, data, and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer empathy and judgment; a structured thinker with a bias for action who&#39;s comfortable with ambiguity and can separate scalable product needs from bespoke requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior-level PM experience, including having built a 0→1 B2B/platform product and worked directly with customers and small engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with recommendation/personalization, growth, monetization, or AI products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial instinct and executive presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in publisher/media tech, adtech, or consumer-growth, or experience productizing internal technology for external customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why Join&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the product foundation for a new AI-native B2B platform, with significant ownership over what NDot becomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn NewsBreak&#39;s capabilities in recommendation, growth, monetization, and AI agents into scalable products — first for publishers, and ultimately for a broader set of digital content businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with customers and a small, high-leverage engineering team to turn real needs into repeatable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
