&lt;li&gt;Build and manage 50+ supplier and rights-holder relationships; lead acquisition negotiations (buyout / minimum guarantee / rev-share), contracts and launch; secure premiere and exclusivity windows; avoid over-exposed catalog titles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creator fund and creator ecosystem (phase 2): once the first wave of China-side supply is live, work with the US Creator Relations lead to design a fund, partnership models and revenue-share rules for US-based creators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track US / China / global charts and audience trends; publish insights for internal teams and creators on what performs with our audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Growth on scaling strategy for titles that win in testing; run post-mortems on hits and misses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and lead content operations, supplier BD and creator relations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in short drama, web fiction or digital video, including 2+ years in content acquisition, distribution or content strategy at an overseas short-drama platform (ReelShort, DramaBox, ShortMax, NetShort, GoodShort, FlexTV, Melolo) or a leading Chinese platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established China-side supply network: existing relationships with studios, AI studios or rights holders, able to start first deals within 30 days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verifiable hit judgment: titles you personally selected or signed that performed, with the data to show why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven: comfortable with completion, conversion and per-title ROI as the basis for decisions, and with having your calls tested and revised&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation and deal-structuring skills across buyout, MG and rev-share models&lt;/li&gt;
