&lt;h3&gt;Why this role exists&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth today comes primarily from recommendation-algorithm tuning and paid acquisition. A product-driven growth curve does not yet exist. This role turns “where is the next curve?” from an open question into a series of hypotheses that can be validated — or disproven — quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native product formats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New ways people consume local information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New direction validation on Scoopz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning vague directions into falsifiable hypotheses, then testing them fast&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handing validated directions to the Senior PM to scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Not local vertical framework build-out&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— a separate team owns that; the boundary is explicit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;must&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years in consumer product&lt;/strong&gt;, including 3+ in 0→1 or new-direction work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;must&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A concrete story where data overturned your own judgment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of killing a direction yourself, with clear reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytics: you pull your own data, design experiments, read results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You instinctively ask “how do users solve this today?” and “what&#39;s the switching cost?”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry open. Consumer high-frequency products preferred (content, social, local, utility)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI product experience not required — the methods transfer, and requiring it only shrinks the pool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;First 90 days&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Form and prioritize 3–5 testable direction hypotheses&lt;/li&gt;
