&lt;li&gt;At least one initiative you started yourself, such as a club, business, research project, campaign, or publication, with results you can show.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication. A short writing sample is requested with your application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with outbound work: calling strangers, running structured interviews, or pitching an idea to someone who did not ask for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency with spreadsheets and with AI tools as a daily working method.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred, Marketing track&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ran a campaign, newsletter, social account, or content project with an audience and measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework or experience in marketing, communications, journalism, or SEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred, Operations track&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in construction, real estate, or home services, including family businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework or experience in economics, statistics, or research methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred, either track&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior internship or work at an early-stage company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Pay may vary based on a number of factors including job-related skills, level, experience, geographic location and relevant education or training. At NewsBreak, we design our overall rewards package to attract top talents. Depending on the position, the role may also be eligible for discretionary bonus and options. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$30&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$60 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/15apsJLgHq1p5NJR3fzFmdctKX4QIzzf2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=110601223912453011659&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CPRA Privacy Notice for California Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NewsBreak&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local life runs on local information.&lt;/strong&gt; What happened down the street? Who can fix this? Where should we go tonight? NewsBreak started in 2015 to answer these questions, and today more than 40 million people a month rely on us to follow what’s going on in their zip code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three platforms with one vision: powering local life.&lt;/strong&gt; Led by founder and CEO Jeff Zheng, NewsBreak is our local life and news platform; Nearby AI connects people with local businesses; and NDot AI helps publishers and creators grow and earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building for the long term.&lt;/strong&gt; A $115 million Series C made us a unicorn in 2021, and we keep investing in our people. We’re Great Place to Work® certified and named to &lt;em&gt;Fast Company&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces for Innovators (2025) and &lt;em&gt;Fortune&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™ (2026).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Everyone makes an impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Whether you write code, shape products, tell our story, or run the business, we want people who own projects end to end, stay curious, and speak up. Join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at: NewsBreak, Nearby AI, NDot AI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt; is a home services platform that connects homeowners with trusted local service providers — plumbers, electricians, cleaners, landscapers, HVAC technicians, and more. We&#39;re building the merchant network that makes that matching possible, and we&#39;re looking for a high-potential MBA intern ready to operate at the level of a founder — not shadow one.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a flagship early-talent initiative at &lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt;: an MBA-level Business Development &amp;amp; Strategy internship built for someone who wants the real thing — full ownership of a merchant-acquisition initiative end-to-end, from market research and territory strategy through self-sourced execution to a final strategic recommendation delivered directly to leadership.&lt;br&gt;There is no script, no shadow assignment, and no busywork. You&#39;ll operate with the autonomy of a strategy consultant and the accountability of a founder — defining your own market thesis, building your own pipeline, and being judged on business outcomes: partners signed, pipeline built, and insight generated that shapes how &lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt; grows.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own, End to End&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Market and Territory Strategy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently map the local service-provider landscape in an assigned category or geography (e.g., HVAC in a specific metro): merchant density, acquisition channels, and competitive platforms (Angi, Thumbtack, Yelp, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build your own scoring framework to size the opportunity and decide which merchant categories or neighborhoods to go after first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Self-Sourced Outreach and Pipeline Development&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build your own target list and figure out the smartest way to reach each one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce &lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt; and pitch the value proposition to local business owners, handling objections yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a pipeline in a CRM or spreadsheet with real discipline: stage, next step, expected close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat outreach as a live experiment — test channels, messaging, and timing, and double down on what the data says is working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Analysis and Business Case Development&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze outreach and conversion data to identify what&#39;s working and quantify results (contacts made, response rates, conversion rates)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn merchant feedback into structured insight that could shape &lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt;&#39;s value proposition or onboarding process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a rigorous business case (expected partners signed, revenue impact) to justify where the company should focus next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Solutioning and Partnership Development&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently draft outreach scripts, pitch decks, and partnership proposals tailored to each merchant type&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead onboarding conversations through to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend improvements to the onboarding process based on what you hear from merchants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Reporting and Recommendations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report weekly on outreach metrics and pipeline, framed as insights and next steps for leadership — not just raw counts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a capstone presentation directly to company leadership: your market analysis, results, and a recommended go-forward strategy for merchant acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re a Strong Fit If You Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing an MBA (or equivalent graduate business program) from a top-tier program, ideally with prior experience in SaaS, agentic services, marketing, sales, BD or a startup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen, critical thinking, and structured problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable being fully self-directed — you build the plan, not just execute someone else&#39;s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for data-driven decision-making; genuinely comfortable working in spreadsheets and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and influencing skills, with the confidence to pick up the phone, knock on a door, and negotiate directly with business owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High tolerance for ambiguity and rejection — energized by 0-to-1, hands-on work, and comfortable inventing your own approach as you go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Type: Internship, 20–40 hrs/week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Duration: 3–6 months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: Paid, $40-60 hourly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://Nearby.ai&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Nearby.ai&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a real merchant-acquisition initiative from research through close, with direct visibility to leadership — a level of end-to-end ownership rarely given to an intern&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with the rigor and stakes of a strategy engagement, at an early-stage company where your work directly moves the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Walk away with a portfolio of quantified business impact (partners signed, pipeline built, a strategy recommendation delivered to leadership) — built for post-MBA BD, strategy, or general management roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Potential to convert to a full-time role based on performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/15apsJLgHq1p5NJR3fzFmdctKX4QIzzf2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=110601223912453011659&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CPRA Privacy Notice for California Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NewsBreak&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local life runs on local information.&lt;/strong&gt; What happened down the street? Who can fix this? Where should we go tonight? NewsBreak started in 2015 to answer these questions, and today more than 40 million people a month rely on us to follow what’s going on in their zip code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three platforms with one vision: powering local life.&lt;/strong&gt; Led by founder and CEO Jeff Zheng, NewsBreak is our local life and news platform; Nearby AI connects people with local businesses; and NDot AI helps publishers and creators grow and earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building for the long term.&lt;/strong&gt; A $115 million Series C made us a unicorn in 2021, and we keep investing in our people. We’re Great Place to Work® certified and named to &lt;em&gt;Fast Company&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces for Innovators (2025) and &lt;em&gt;Fortune&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™ (2026).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Everyone makes an impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Whether you write code, shape products, tell our story, or run the business, we want people who own projects end to end, stay curious, and speak up. Join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at: NewsBreak, Nearby AI, NDot AI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a curious, technically strong software engineer to join our Corporate Ventures and AI Operations team. This is a hybrid role sitting at the intersection of backend engineering, ML infrastructure, and revenue systems — you&#39;ll build and maintain the pipelines and services that power our ads platform, engineer the recommendation systems that keep users coming back, build the tools that automate commission and quota-setting for our ad sales team, and work closely with business stakeholders to ship production systems that turn data into decisions. You care about the milliseconds between a user opening the app and finding something they love. You think about what makes someone stay, subscribe, and come back tomorrow — and you write the code that makes that happen at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audience Retention &amp;amp; Performance Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build instrumentation and monitoring systems that track performance signals (load times, stream quality, error rates) to ensure users experience fast, flawless products across web, app, and live streams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to backend services and dashboards that track engagement and retention metrics — session length, scroll depth, return rate, and drop-off points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling to help surface friction in the user journey, working with product and engineering to ship fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the experimentation infrastructure used to test retention-boosting product changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recommendation &amp;amp; Personalization Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to recommendation algorithms and services that surface the right content to the right user at the right moment, under the guidance of senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the data infrastructure (feature pipelines, training datasets, feedback loops) that keeps recommendation models fresh, accurate, and served in production with low latency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help instrument personalization systems to measure impact on session time, click-through rates, and long-term retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with content and product teams to ship recommendation output into intuitive, performant user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Backend Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain components of data pipelines and services that process large-scale ads, user event, and engagement data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-tested code (SQL, Python, PySpark, or similar) to transform raw data into reliable, analysis-ready datasets and APIs, with code review support from senior team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the data architecture supporting ad-tech integrations, paywall flows, and subscription checkout — helping ensure these monetization surfaces are instrumented, reliable, fast, and resilient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build automated checks to monitor data quality and flag data integrity issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with platform and engineering teams to keep systems scalable, observable, and well-documented&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue Operations Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the engineering behind the commission calculation system for the ad sales team, with a senior engineer owning overall design — focusing on accuracy, reliability, and auditability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build tools that support sales quota-setting, working alongside senior engineers and Finance partners who own the underlying business logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to simulation tools that model commission payout scenarios and the cost/incentive impact of quota and comp plan changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional partners (product, marketing, sales) to understand their tooling needs and help ship solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build alerting to surface trends and anomalies in ads performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help automate recurring operational reporting to free up team bandwidth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree (recent grad or up to ~2 years of experience) in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid software engineering fundamentals — data structures, algorithms, basic system design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one general-purpose programming language (Python, Java, Scala, or Go) and working knowledge of SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework, academic projects, or internship experience involving data pipelines, backend services, or applied software systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to distributed data processing concepts (Spark, Hive, or similar) is a plus, not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic understanding of A/B testing and experimental design principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a competitive benefits package:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health, dental, and vision care for you and your family (100% coverage for employee)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Top-tier 401(K) plan with company matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid time off and paid holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FSA, HSA and commuter benefits programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team activity budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is listed below. Pay may vary based on a number of factors including job-related skills, level, experience, geographic location and relevant education or training. At NewsBreak, we design our overall rewards package to attract top talents. Depending on the position, the role may also be eligible for discretionary bonus and options. Your recruiter can share more details during the hiring process.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Base Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$135,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$155,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/15apsJLgHq1p5NJR3fzFmdctKX4QIzzf2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=110601223912453011659&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CPRA Privacy Notice for California Candidates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NewsBreak&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Local life runs on local information.&lt;/strong&gt; What happened down the street? Who can fix this? Where should we go tonight? NewsBreak started in 2015 to answer these questions, and today more than 40 million people a month rely on us to follow what’s going on in their zip code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three platforms with one vision: powering local life.&lt;/strong&gt; Led by founder and CEO Jeff Zheng, NewsBreak is our local life and news platform; Nearby AI connects people with local businesses; and NDot AI helps publishers and creators grow and earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building for the long term.&lt;/strong&gt; A $115 million Series C made us a unicorn in 2021, and we keep investing in our people. We’re Great Place to Work® certified and named to &lt;em&gt;Fast Company&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces for Innovators (2025) and &lt;em&gt;Fortune&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™ (2026).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Everyone makes an impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Whether you write code, shape products, tell our story, or run the business, we want people who own projects end to end, stay curious, and speak up. Join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at: NewsBreak, Nearby AI, NDot AI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a core member of our growing HR team, you will help build NewsBreak&#39;s HR infrastructure from the ground up, supporting both our main business and newly incubated businesses. You won&#39;t just design and implement conventional HR programs; we want you to think outside the box and keep finding new ways to attract and retain top talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Partner Rewards &amp;amp; Experience, you will build and run the engine behind how we rewards, develops and listens to people. You will own the annual performance and compensation review, benefits administration, total rewards infrastructure, HR policies, and employee experience such as onboarding experience and engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe our policies, pay structure and benefits are a reflection of our culture. Rolling out a policy or a performance cycle can be purely operational: stating the facts clearly and moving on. We are looking for someone who goes further, a cultural ambassador within the HR who brings the values behind each program to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder role in a fast-moving start-up company. You will turn recurring cycles into reliable, well-documented processes, and turn people data into insights leaders act on. You will work closely with HR leaders, Finance, Legal and business leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review salary bands against market benchmark data and recommend range adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain job architecture: job families, levels and leveling guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the annual equity refresh and administer the equity program (grants, vesting, employee communication) with Finance and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track benefits cost, utilization and renewal trends for plan design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Annual performance &amp;amp; compensation review&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the annual performance review cycle: calendar, system setup, manager and employee enablement, completion tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run 360 feedback, facilitate performance calibration meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the promotion process: criteria, nominations, calibration and approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the annual compensation review: merit, bonus and promotion budgets, guidelines matrix, modeling and manager recommendations, work in both Workday or any other related system/tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits administration&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer health, welfare and retirement plans; lead annual open enrollment, carrier and broker coordination, and plan renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor SLAs, escalations and invoice reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate benefits plan filings and notices (e.g., ACA reporting, COBRA) with the vendor and broker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR policies&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own HR policies including drafting, updating and maintaining the employee handbook and HR policies (compensation, leave, time off, expenses, remote work etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal on policy review and communicate changes clearly to employees and leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go beyond the facts when presenting policies, performance and pay programs: use case studies and real examples to show the culture and values behind them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee experience &amp;amp; culture&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver new-hire onboarding covering business, products, mission and culture; coordinate leader speakers and measure new-hire experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run the company-wide engagement survey; analyze results, share insights with leadership, and track action plans to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-bring&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in compensation, benefits, or HR COE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working on building and administrating salary band, benchmarking, bonus and equity program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing annual performance and merit/bonus/equity refresh cycle end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of benefits regulations (e.g., FMLA, COBRA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience administering US benefits programs through an external vendor/broker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging, high-energy presenter and clear writer; able to bring pay, performance and policy programs to life for employees and executives, not just explain the facts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High integrity and discretion with confidential data.&lt;/li&gt;
