&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building for the long term.&lt;/strong&gt; A $115 million Series C made us a unicorn in 2021, and we keep investing in our people. We’re Great Place to Work® certified and named to &lt;em&gt;Fast Company&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces for Innovators (2025) and &lt;em&gt;Fortune&lt;/em&gt;’s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™ (2026).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Everyone makes an impact.&lt;/strong&gt; Whether you write code, shape products, tell our story, or run the business, we want people who own projects end to end, stay curious, and speak up. Join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more at: NewsBreak, Nearby AI, NDot AI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why this role exists&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team has a Lead, and direction is well set — the agentic system is their initiative. But that same person also heads the part-time jobs vertical. Two significant roles, one person&#39;s bandwidth means the time available for paid growth is limited. Day-to-day operations are covered by a colleague who is new to growth — at this budget scale, incrementality judgment, bidding strategy, and experiment design sit beyond their current experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s missing isn&#39;t direction; it&#39;s an experienced operator running the function full-time.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;That colleague will continue on execution under you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That explains the present state: no incrementality testing has ever been run, a hyper-local product bids uniformly nationwide, angle tests run without pre-registered sample sizes or stopping rules, and close to half the team still performs work the platforms have automated. Conservatively, eight figures of annual efficiency sits unclaimed here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platform automation has absorbed most manual optimization headroom — the ceiling isn&#39;t operational precision.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Experiment design and analytical judgment are the core skills; knowing the Meta interface is table stakes.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-channel budget reallocation grounded in incrementality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standardizing how angles get tested&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— the most concrete gap today: pre-registered sample sizes and power calculations, success criteria and stopping rules set before launch, a consistent control, a structured test log, and strict&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;separation&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;of message tests from creative tests (never vary both). Testing happens today, but conclusions are of uncertain reliability: the true hit rate is unknown, and winners may have been killed while noise was kept&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guardrails and supervision for the agentic bidding system&lt;/strong&gt;: approval thresholds, audit logs, rollback, enforced holdouts, and when to trust it versus intervene. The Lead sets system direction; this role owns rollout and risk control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rollout of geo-tiered bidding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extracting platform support — at this spend level you should have rep support, lift studies, and alpha access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rebalancing the team: nearly half of it still does work the platforms have automated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;must&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years in app UA, having independently run $30M+ per year&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— small-budget experience doesn&#39;t transfer; this bar is firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;must&quot;&gt;You can answer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;“Given a system that reallocates budget automatically, how do you stop it from moving spend toward zero-incrementality inventory?”&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve cut spend that looked good in the dashboard but wasn&#39;t incremental&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You design your own experiments, including power calculations and stopping rules&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve managed 4+ people, including at least one non-buying function (analytics, creative, or engineering)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry open&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;block lang-en&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;First 90 days&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit optimization events: how much budget sits on installs versus downstream value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With the Growth DS, translate the first incrementality readout into actual budget shifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up the two-layer testing framework and ring-fence an exploration budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
